# Introduction

A tiny perl snippet counts the words in a sentence. Nothing is silenced here, so every chunk shows its code.

# Counting

```{perl}
my $text = "one two three";
my @words = split / /, $text;
print scalar(@words), "\n";
```

# Longest Word

```{r}
words <- c("one", "two", "three")
words[which.max(nchar(words))]
```

```

# Sorting

The words are sorted alphabetically in the next chunk.

```{perl}
my @sorted = sort ("pear", "apple", "fig");
print join(" ", @sorted), "\n";
```

# Lookup

```{r}
match("fig", c("pear", "apple", "fig"))
```

# Reversal

```{perl}
print scalar reverse("abc"), "\n";
```

# Closing

That is all for the word-count examples.

